From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 07:11:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 103/184] segacd: the sector cache indexed three megabytes past
 itself

D: has been handing GEMDOS blocks that never came off the disc, and
reporting perfect health while doing it. Under gpgx: Fread on
READCD.TXT returning 32 bytes of zeroes, and Dfree reporting 348 free
clusters on a volume with 92 -- a difference of exactly 256, which in
FAT16 is exactly one 512-byte block of the table read as zeroes.
Meanwhile err 0, why 0000, no torn headers, no wrong sectors, and
cdc_grab reporting the sector arrived with all 512 of its longs
nonzero. Every counter in the driver was telling the truth. The loss
was after them.

cd_fetch calls cdc_setup on its first attempt, and cdc_setup
invalidates the cache -- rightly, it is resetting the decoder and
moving the drive. But cd_fill set cd_cache_base before its read-ahead
and then updated only cd_cache_have inside the loop, so every
successful read-ahead left the pair reading "six sectors starting at
0xFFFFFFFF". The hand-off indexes cd_cache by lba minus that base:
1614 minus 0xFFFFFFFF is 1615, an index into a six-element array. It
copied 512 bytes from three megabytes past the end and called it a
sector.

Two changes. cd_fill publishes base and have once, after the fill,
never before. And each slot now records which sector is actually in
it, so the hand-off checks the index instead of trusting the
subtraction -- an index it cannot justify is a failed read, not a copy
from wherever it points. That check is the thing that found this: it
fired five times a round with want 1600 got -1, and the base and have
latched beside it said 0xFFFFFFFF and 6.

Under gpgx, four rounds: Dfree 92 every time, Fread returns the file
every time, and the invariant never fires. Before, round one read
zeroes and Dfree alternated 348 and 92. PicoDrive still boots and
runs.

The instrumentation stays. It costs a hundred cycles a block and it
is the only reason a fault this quiet was found at all -- along with
ring/dsr/edt/nz counters, the mode-gate count, and the raw bytes of
every Fread, all of which the console will now report too.
---
 bios/bios.c   |  30 ++++++++
 bios/segacd.c | 198 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 bios/segacd.h |   5 ++
 3 files changed, 222 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bios/bios.c b/bios/bios.c
index 5e8d88e..517d0f9 100644
--- a/bios/bios.c
+++ b/bios/bios.c
@@ -1158,6 +1158,11 @@ void biosmain(void)
